in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @spectral
in @spectral/gen_prism
in @spectral/supervisor
in @uuid/spectral

# @spectral/parent — the single-parent lifecycle edge type.
#
# THE FOURTH SUB-SHARD of the @spectral runtime cascade. Sibling of
# `shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror` (commit ae965ca, the worker
# primitive whose `parent: uuid_spectral` field this shard types at
# the edge altitude), `shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror` (commit
# 452ccb2, the lifecycle-owner whose `start_child` sets the parent
# edge on spawn), and `shards/spectral/registry.mirror` (commit
# 489211e, the supervisor's typed child index — the registry indexes
# CHILDREN of a supervisor; the parent edge points the OTHER WAY).
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3-4 (2026-06-10, Mara): every
# gen_prism has exactly one parent. The parent edge is the LIFECYCLE
# edge: the parent owns the child's birth, restart, and death. The
# parent-edge class is ACYCLIC across the substrate. The root
# supervisor self-parents (its parent uuid_spectral byte-equals its
# identity); every non-root gen_prism's parent points strictly
# upward toward the root.
#
# === The forward-promise this tick closes ===
#
# `shards/spectral/registry.mirror` (commit 489211e) declared:
#
#   "shards/spectral/parent.mirror   single-parent lifecycle edge
#                                    type (acyclic). STOP-condition
#                                    2/4: the acyclic invariant
#                                    wants its own property/fracture
#                                    bilateral pair (analogous to
#                                    `keyword_matches_depth` per
#                                    [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]).
#                                    That's a separate bilateral
#                                    instance, not a simple type
#                                    declaration; it lands as its
#                                    own tick;"
#
# That tick is this tick. The PARENT EDGE TYPE lands here; the
# acyclic invariant lands as a sibling property + fracture body
# pair at:
#
#   shards/epistemologic/property/parent_acyclic.mirror
#     (the declarative half — the predicate that surfaces cycle
#      opacities)
#   shards/kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle.mirror
#     (the operational half — the fracture body that proposes
#      re-parenting the offending child to the root supervisor)
#
# Together: instance 6 of bilateral pattern #53 (promoted; per
# [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]). Prior instances:
# 1=keyword (5e68df9 + d908798), 2=gate (b8755cc + 20c5d97),
# 3=symbol (95f4639 + f083a55), 4=partials_align (meta-fracture;
# fd344bf + 5c4e3ca), 5=operator_match (423c7d2 + af670d4). This
# instance lands the bilateral at the GRAPH-EDGE altitude — the
# first instance whose subject is a SUBSTRATE EDGE rather than a
# token/literal/symbol position. Recognition #59 (kintsugi loop is
# altitude-portable; promoted with af670d4) gains a new witness:
# the bilateral signature scales not just across declaration
# altitudes (keyword/operator/symbol) but to GRAPH STRUCTURE
# (parent edge acyclic invariant).
#
# === The keyword decision ===
#
# `glass` per recognition #46 (path-syntax property; promoted) and
# `shards/spectral.mirror`'s discipline section: "@spectral
# sub-shards at depth >= 1 use `glass`; the family root itself uses
# `prism` per the depth-0 discipline."
#
# Why NOT a new substrate keyword: parent is an EDGE TYPE — a typed
# relation between gen_prisms — and `glass` already names that at
# the sub-prism altitude per `shards/glass.mirror`'s
# `glass(name) -> prism` form. Same reasoning as gen_prism
# (ae965ca), supervisor (452ccb2), and registry (489211e): not a
# new structural kind, but a typed edge over existing carriers
# (uuid_spectral on both endpoints).
#
# === The parent_edge shape ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3: the parent edge points
# child → parent. The substrate's load-bearing carrier for both
# endpoints is `uuid_spectral`. The dark 80 bits identify the
# process; both endpoints discriminate on byte-equality of the
# dark portion (the same identity_signal the registry's `lookup`
# discriminates on per shards/spectral/registry.mirror).
#
#   child   — `uuid_spectral`. The owned gen_prism's identity. The
#              direction-of-ownership convention: the parent OWNS
#              lifecycle of the child; the edge points FROM the
#              child to its lifecycle-owner. The field name reads
#              as a record key naming the child-side of the edge.
#   parent  — `uuid_spectral`. The owning gen_prism's identity. The
#              parentage destination. For the root supervisor,
#              `child == parent` byte-equally (the root self-parents;
#              the substrate's parentless-vocabulary anchor per
#              docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3 — at ~/.mirror/).
#              For every NON-root gen_prism, `child != parent` and
#              the chain of parent traversals terminates at the
#              root in a bounded number of steps.
#
# The type is small. The substrate's load-bearing structure is the
# acyclic INVARIANT, not the record shape. The property/fracture
# bilateral pair (sibling shards in this tick) is what makes the
# invariant operational.
#
# === Why a typed edge record (not just the gen_prism.parent field) ===
#
# The gen_prism record (shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror line 257-261)
# already carries a `parent: uuid_spectral` field. Why declare a
# separate `parent_edge` record here?
#
# Substrate-pull-correct rationale:
#
#   - The gen_prism.parent FIELD is the per-gen_prism CARRIER of
#     the parent identity (one parent per gen_prism by record
#     shape). This is the gen_prism's INTERNAL surface.
#
#   - The parent_edge RECORD is the substrate-altitude REIFIED
#     EDGE between two gen_prisms (child uuid + parent uuid as one
#     record). This is the substrate's EXTERNAL surface — the
#     edge as a first-class substrate object the property's
#     predicate ranges over.
#
# The predicate at the sibling property
# (`parent_acyclic(file: ref) -> transparency`) reads the set of
# parent_edges as `[parent_edge]` — a list of typed edge records.
# Without the reified record, the predicate would have to range
# over `[gen_prism]` and project `.parent` per element, which
# conflates the carrier (the gen_prism) with the structural
# question (the edge graph). Same logic as `registry_entry` in
# shards/spectral/registry.mirror: the registry COULD inline the
# entry as `(uuid_spectral, gen_prism)` pairs, but the typed
# record makes the registry's query surface readable.
#
# Per [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]: every
# load-bearing substrate concept gets its own typed declaration.
# The parent edge IS such a concept (the supervision tree's
# single-direction lifecycle edge); it deserves its own type.
#
# === Orthogonal to entanglement ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §4: entanglement is the
# peer-correlation edge class, ORTHOGONAL to parentage. The two
# edge classes:
#
#   parent_edge      directed; child → parent; one-per-child;
#                     ACYCLIC across the substrate; lifecycle-
#                     owning; the supervisor acts on this edge.
#   entanglement     polyadic (N-ary); peer correlation; many-per-
#                     gen_prism; cyclic permitted; observational;
#                     sheaf restriction map at substrate altitude
#                     (cellular sheaf per [[Eigenboard is a sheaf]]).
#
# The acyclic INVARIANT applies to parent_edges ALONE. Entanglement
# edges may cycle freely (mutual entanglement is the common case:
# Mara's spawn entangles with the mirror repo gen_prism; the mirror
# repo gen_prism entangles with Mara's spawn — symmetric peer
# correlation). The substrate NEVER conflates the two edge classes;
# the property at `parent_acyclic.mirror` ranges over parent_edges
# ONLY (not entanglement edges).
#
# This is STOP-condition 4 from the brief, resolved: parent and
# entanglement share gen_prism vocabulary (both endpoint sets are
# uuid_spectral-typed) but NOT the invariant. The parent_acyclic
# property doesn't need to reference entanglement edges to
# distinguish them; the edge-class is named structurally by the
# type itself. `parent_edge` is its own substrate-altitude type;
# `entanglement` will be its own substrate-altitude type at its
# own sibling shard.
#
# === Sheaf reading: registry's degenerate reading, NOT this shard ===
#
# Per shards/spectral/registry.mirror §"Sheaf reading: NOT here, it's
# at entanglement" and [[Eigenboard is a sheaf]]: the cellular-sheaf
# restriction-map structure lives at the ENTANGLEMENT edge class.
# The registry's typed surface stays at the index discipline; the
# parent edge's typed surface stays at the lifecycle discipline.
# This is STOP-condition 2 from the brief, resolved: parent is a
# typed EDGE (the lifecycle invariant carrier), not a sheaf
# restriction map. The sheaf reading is downstream of substrate at
# entanglement.
#
# Architectural note (NOT a STOP): one could read parent_edge as a
# DEGENERATE sheaf — each edge IS a restriction map from the
# parent's eigenboard slice to the child's eigenboard slice along
# the lifecycle direction. That reading is consistent with
# [[Eigenboard is a sheaf]]'s cellular-sheaf framing but NOT
# load-bearing at this tick. The substrate's sheaf surface lives at
# entanglement; the parent's typed surface stays at the lifecycle
# invariant.
#
# === Honest partial discipline (per #306) ===
#
# This shard declares a TYPE (parent_edge) only. No action bodies,
# no `\` obligations, no fracture body emitted by this shard. The
# property's predicate and the fracture body's morphism emission
# live at the sibling shards; their honest `partials` accounting is
# computed in those shards.
#
# === Cascade siblings (forward-promised, NOT landing this tick) ===
#
#   shards/spectral/entanglement.mirror   peer correlation edge;
#                                          sheaf restriction map at
#                                          substrate altitude
#                                          (cellular sheaf per
#                                          [[Eigenboard is a sheaf]]);
#                                          polyadic; cyclic permitted;
#                                          orthogonal to parent;
#   shards/spectral/root.mirror           parentless supervisor;
#                                          vocabulary anchor at
#                                          ~/.mirror/; the substrate's
#                                          self-parented top of the
#                                          parent-edge graph;
#   shards/spectral/portal.mirror         runtime side of portal
#                                          (gen_prism specialisation
#                                          carrying the frame stream).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md (the ouroboros
#               spec; §3 supervision tree — parent is the lifecycle
#               edge; §4 entanglement graph — parent is orthogonal
#               to entanglement; §8 cascade map).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-three-tier-stack]] (the
#                      SpectralSupervisor precedent; the supervision
#                      tree this edge type structures),
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                      (this tick's parent_edge type + sibling
#                      property/fracture pair are instance 6 of the
#                      bilateral pattern; the first instance at the
#                      graph-edge altitude),
#                      [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] (the parent
#                      edge is set at start_child; the registry
#                      shard advances by one settle when a parent
#                      edge is established),
#                      [[Eigenboard is a sheaf]] (the architectural
#                      surface: sheaf restriction maps live at
#                      entanglement, NOT parent; degenerate sheaf
#                      reading of the parent edge surfaced but not
#                      load-bearing),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the parent edge was named informally at
#                      spectral.mirror line 116-118 and at
#                      gen_prism.mirror line 244-249 since the
#                      family root landed; this tick names the edge
#                      at the substrate altitude — another instance
#                      of the rug-pull pattern).
# Related shards: spectral.mirror (the family root this glass is
#                  under),
#                 spectral/gen_prism.mirror (the gen_prism's parent
#                  field is typed uuid_spectral; this shard names
#                  the typed EDGE over those fields; commit ae965ca),
#                 spectral/supervisor.mirror (the lifecycle-owner
#                  whose start_child sets the parent edge on spawn;
#                  commit 452ccb2),
#                 spectral/registry.mirror (the supervisor's child
#                  index; the registry indexes children of a
#                  supervisor, the parent edge points the OTHER WAY;
#                  commit 489211e),
#                 uuid/spectral.mirror (the identity carrier at both
#                  endpoints of the edge; the dark 80 bits
#                  discriminate),
#                 epistemologic/property/parent_acyclic.mirror
#                  (sibling tick; the declarative half of bilateral
#                  instance 6 — the property over the set of
#                  parent_edges in the substrate),
#                 kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle.mirror (sibling
#                  tick; the operational half of bilateral instance
#                  6 — the fracture body that proposes re-parenting
#                  to the root when a cycle is detected).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/spectral/parent.mirror` declares `@spectral/parent` and
# only that.

glass @spectral/parent {
  focus parent
  project parent
  split parent
  shift parent
  settle parent
}

# === parent_edge — one lifecycle edge ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3 — the supervision tree's
# single-direction lifecycle edge. One record per gen_prism (every
# gen_prism has exactly one parent edge; the root supervisor's edge
# is the self-parent).
#
#   child   — the owned gen_prism's uuid_spectral. The lookup key
#              for "which edge does this gen_prism's parent live
#              on?" Discrimination is on byte-equality of the dark
#              80 bits (the identity_signal per
#              shards/uuid/spectral.mirror).
#   parent  — the owning gen_prism's uuid_spectral. The destination
#              of the edge. For the root supervisor, byte-equals
#              `child`; for every other gen_prism, points strictly
#              upward toward the root via a chain that terminates
#              at the root in a bounded number of steps (the
#              acyclic invariant the sibling property declares).
#
# The edge is REIFIED as a record so the sibling property's
# predicate can range over `[parent_edge]` — the substrate-altitude
# external surface of the supervision tree's edge graph.
type parent_edge = {
  child:  uuid_spectral,
  parent: uuid_spectral,
}

out @spectral/parent
out parent_edge
